# Line endings. Store and check out text files with LF (Unix) line endings, even when they are
# edited on Windows (VS Code, Notepad, ...). Without this, a file saved with CRLF shows up in diffs
# as "every line changed", and a CRLF inside a setter comment or script can break tools.
* text=auto eol=lf

# SOPS-encrypted files: git must never rewrite their bytes. SOPS adds a MAC over the file's content,
# and these were encrypted with CRLF; leave them exactly as they are (re-encrypting one with sops
# writes it with LF, which is fine).
secret.*.yaml -text
# cluster-issuer.yaml is SOPS-encrypted too (its email); not named secret.* because it isn't a Secret.
apps/network/cluster-issuer.yaml -text

# Binary files: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
